  "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
  "label": "Harmful",
  "description": "The image and text together may be interpreted as reinforcing harmful stereotypes about Black people, particularly through the visual presentation of the central figure in what could be seen as stereotypical or exoticized attire, combined with the crowd's reaction. The overlay text 'peace is love' does not inherently contain toxicity, but when mapped onto the visual of the Black man (mapping_1), it can be seen as a form of performative or symbolic appropriation that may unintentionally or intentionally reinforce the very stereotypes the text seeks to counteract. The analogical mapping projects the message of peace onto a figure whose appearance and context may trigger historical racial stereotypes, thus creating a potentially harmful effect by normalizing or trivializing the racialized presentation of the subject.",
